{"name":"Secrecy","hex":"#50759e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"secrecy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Concealment; the condition of being secret or hidden.","The habit of keeping secrets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secrecy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Secrecy","blocks":[{"text":"Secrecy is the practice of hiding information from certain individuals or groups who do not have the \"need to know\", perhaps while sharing it with other individuals. That which is kept hidden is known as the secret."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg/330px-If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secrecy","wikidata":"Q1503443"},{"title":"Secrecy (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Secrecy is a 1997 novel and New York Times bestseller by Belva Plain. It tells the story of Charlotte, a little girl from the Dawes family whose adolescence life was shattered after she was raped by Ted, her uncle's stepson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Secrecy_%28book%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secrecy_(book)","wikidata":"Q7443921"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/500px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/1280px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg/500px-Loose_lips_might_sink_ships.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","